  "result": "I fixed the open-bound clamping bug in `IntRange`. Clamped values now stay inside the range.\n\n- **Fix:** In `src/click/types.py`, `IntRange._clamp` now returns `bound + dir` instead of `bound - dir`. Previously, `IntRange(0, min_open=True, clamp=True)` turned `-1` into `-1`, which is still outside the range. It now gives `1`. `IntRange(max=5, max_open=True, clamp=True)` turned `6` into `5`, which is also excluded. It now gives `4`.\n- **Tests:** I added both cases to the `test_range` parametrization in `tests/test_types.py`.\n- **Results:** `pytest tests/test_types.py tests/test_info_dict.py` passes: 71 passed, 2 skipped.\n\nI didn't commit anything. The change is only in the working tree.",
